#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""kb-money-radar — scheduled daily money-opportunity radar.

Spec: project-local money-radar runtime spec v6,
approved sha256:9bc0a18e4b5f49d6d8c4b784d150daedcfc160e7b6d959556a468106e66f74c8.

Runs every rostered opportunity-search agent read-only in parallel, captures each
agent's structured candidate payload, deterministically merges/dedups/labels
confidence/validates/ranks, renders a report + an owner-language digest, and (when
telegram is requested) delivers it through kb-channel-send. No LLM synthesis step;
the orchestrator is the only writer and writes only an allowlist of dated paths.

Scheduled roster (OS-safe only): Codex (--sandbox read-only) + Claude
(--permission-mode plan + --allowedTools Read,Glob,Grep). The Grok/Antigravity
social lane is roster-defined but disabled in background unless --with-social.

Env:
  KB_HUB                       hub root (default ~/knowledge)
  MONEY_RADAR_PROJECT          project root (defaults to cwd only when cwd has knowledge/)
  KB_PROCESS_OUTPUTS           telegram,file (set by kb-tick)
  KB_PROCESS_BACKGROUND        1 in scheduled runs (gates social/web adapters)
  MONEY_RADAR_<ID>_BIN         per-adapter binary override (id upper, '-'->'_')
  MONEY_RADAR_<ID>_TIMEOUT     per-adapter real-pass timeout override (seconds)
  MONEY_RADAR_CHANNEL_BIN      kb-channel-send override (tests)
  MONEY_RADAR_CURL_BIN         curl override (tests)
"""
